WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.290
There will be organizational beams.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.720
Inside, these beams here relate to the small wing here.

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.729
You see, these are very important lines of force.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.260
But at the moment you have primitive cephalic flexion,

5
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.610
you will have the sub-mesencephalic mesenchyme compressed between the anterior part

6
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:25.750
of the brain vesicle and the posterior brain vesicle.

7
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.040
This is at the beginning.

8
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.640
My tissue is like this.

9
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.810
And through the flexion movement,

10
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:38.070
I move forward. The mesenchyme below, will undergo a compression field on its axis,

11
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:45.583
It will lose water, it will densify and it becomes cartilaginous tissue.

12
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:49.980
This is how the base of the skull forms. Through the flexion movement.

13
00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.258
With as an axis, always,

14
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.780
my notochord.

15
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.700
And on either side, I have what we call at the top the ethmoid,

16
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.010
just below the body of the sphenoid,

17
00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:08.390
below that the basilar part of the occipital bone, and especially here what we call

18
00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:12.550
the wings of the sphenoid, but also the point where the eye will settle.

19
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.560
It's the support of the eye, the sphenoid.

20
00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:21.280
is very important for the stability of the eye.

21
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.600
As it grows, the mesenchyme...

22
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.650
that is above, the bony capsule of the eye, will develop through the growth of the

23
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.680
brain, around the eye.

24
00:01:33.531 --> 00:01:38.651
So the eye is there, it follows the movement, it is conforming and conformed,

25
00:01:40.811 --> 00:01:46.181
and the bony tissue comes to encase around it, comes to close with specific lines of

26
00:01:46.181 --> 00:01:48.681
force that support the support of the eye.

27
00:01:48.681 --> 00:01:52.091
This means that the eye can destabilize the skull

28
00:01:52.281 --> 00:01:55.571
or the skull can destabilize the eye. You see?

29
00:01:55.721 --> 00:02:01.181
A small bump, a little fringe can completely destabilize the orbit and completely

30
00:02:01.181 --> 00:02:03.241
destabilize the reflection, you see?

31
00:02:03.761 --> 00:02:07.451
So it's really important to arrive at re-stabilizing the eye,

32
00:02:07.451 --> 00:02:10.741
to understand it both by the brain and by the skull.

33
00:02:10.741 --> 00:02:11.861
This is your nose.

34
00:02:13.161 --> 00:02:14.451
It's going to grow. Bam!

35
00:02:14.451 --> 00:02:17.811
And there, we see the eye appearing on the side.

36
00:02:17.811 --> 00:02:21.511
And you see, at the same time, I have the palate system forming.

37
00:02:21.511 --> 00:02:23.711
At the moment I have my eye forming,

38
00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:28.148
my palate is coming into place. You see?

39
00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.728
Really with the closure.

40
00:02:29.728 --> 00:02:31.968
The palatine, here, comes in.

41
00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:36.598
And when I have completely my eye having found its axis in its verticality,

42
00:02:36.598 --> 00:02:39.708
in its horizontality, I have the palate formed.

43
00:02:40.271 --> 00:02:42.191
So it is really the point terminal

44
00:02:43.991 --> 00:02:48.292
very important on the bony level that is forming. It's a first convergence.

45
00:02:48.422 --> 00:02:52.622
So we see here, you see, the growth, the importance of this growth.

46
00:02:52.782 --> 00:02:54.702
And look at the cephalic part.

47
00:02:55.602 --> 00:03:00.002
It is at the moment when this cephalic part will really begin to grow that the eyes

48
00:03:00.002 --> 00:03:01.869
come closer to the midline.

49
00:03:01.902 --> 00:03:05.967
Look carefully, with a support point that will form at the level of the Nasion.

50
00:03:09.362 --> 00:03:11.282
Look now at the white part.

51
00:03:15.182 --> 00:03:16.528
I am growing.

52
00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:19.432
Now, I explode.

53
00:03:22.292 --> 00:03:24.532
The eyes come back toward the midline.

54
00:03:30.292 --> 00:03:35.492
Did you see? We see again this biodynamics or this morphogenetics of development.

55
00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:42.512
This huge growth that comes from here.

56
00:03:45.502 --> 00:03:48.222
that makes my eyes come to the center.

57
00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:54.902
The cortical development directs the eye in its position. You will have two spirals.

58
00:03:57.202 --> 00:03:58.802
One spiral of the eye

59
00:04:00.342 --> 00:04:02.732
and one counter-spiral of bone.

60
00:04:06.302 --> 00:04:08.622
You see this in the shape of the sutures.

61
00:04:08.622 --> 00:04:12.592
If you look closely, you need to study the orientation of this suture.

62
00:04:12.633 --> 00:04:15.913
And you see that this premaxilla is three-dimensional.

63
00:04:18.413 --> 00:04:20.103
You see, it does this.

64
00:04:20.103 --> 00:04:23.123
goes up, it goes down, and it goes back up.

65
00:04:23.123 --> 00:04:26.243
And it really creates a three-dimensionality.

66
00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:31.663
And well, you see that it forms, this shape, orbital, ocular.

